From e75845b1f0efc311d64c9570737c4f404d072c33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Tarabocchia <connorcjcj11@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 20:43:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webrtc-sys: never hand a video receiver a null frame
 transformer

The detach in ~FrameCryptor (73ff28c) cleared the transformer on the
RtpReceiver so the FrameCryptorTransformer thread could be reclaimed. That
is what libwebrtc's audio receiver expects a null to mean. Its video
receiver does not: RtpVideoStreamReceiver2::SetDepacketizerToDecoderFrameTransformer
wraps the argument in a RtpVideoStreamReceiverFrameTransformerDelegate and
calls Init(), which dereferences it -- SIGSEGV on the worker thread,
measured 2026-09-08 the first time a subscribed video track's cryptor was
dropped (KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS at 0x0 in
RtpVideoStreamReceiverFrameTransformerDelegate::Init, called from
~FrameCryptor on a tokio worker).

Detach audio receivers as before; leave a video receiver's transformer
attached, which is the behaviour before 73ff28c for those tracks only.
Senders are unchanged: the video send path recreates its stream on a
transformer change and takes a null.
---
 webrtc-sys/src/frame_cryptor.cpp | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/webrtc-sys/src/frame_cryptor.cpp b/webrtc-sys/src/frame_cryptor.cpp
index 2cf2282..cbb9dec 100644
--- a/webrtc-sys/src/frame_cryptor.cpp
+++ b/webrtc-sys/src/frame_cryptor.cpp
@@ -177,8 +177,21 @@ FrameCryptor::~FrameCryptor() {
   if (sender_) {
     sender_->SetEncoderToPacketizerFrameTransformer(nullptr);
   }
+  // Receivers: audio only. libwebrtc's audio receiver treats a null
+  // transformer as "none"; its video receiver (RtpVideoStreamReceiver2)
+  // wraps whatever it is handed in a RtpVideoStreamReceiverFrameTransformerDelegate
+  // and dereferences it in Init(), so a null there is a segfault on the
+  // worker thread the moment a video cryptor is destroyed -- which is every
+  // unsubscribe, every remote unpublish and every room close once a video
+  // track has been received. A video receiver therefore keeps its
+  // transformer attached until the peer connection goes, the pre-patch
+  // behaviour, and leaks that one thread per video track per room; the
+  // audio receivers, which are every call, are still reclaimed.
   if (receiver_) {
-    receiver_->SetDepacketizerToDecoderFrameTransformer(nullptr);
+    auto track = receiver_->track();
+    if (track && track->kind() == "audio") {
+      receiver_->SetDepacketizerToDecoderFrameTransformer(nullptr);
+    }
   }
 }
 
